# Configuration variables deliberately NOT in Config_Tag, with the reason.
#
# Config_Tag names every variable a COMPILED unit can read, so that two
# configurations differing only in one of them cannot share an adalib and
# silently reuse each other's objects (CONTRACT.md 7.11). The variables below
# reach only the LINKER -- they become -Wl,--defsym= values, so they change the
# link line and not a single object file. Tagging them would fork the whole
# runtime library on a value no compiled unit can observe.
#
# Anything not listed here must appear in Config_Tag. populate.sh enforces that
# against Alire's own build_hash_inputs, so a newly added variable fails the
# populate until someone decides which side it belongs on.
#
# DDR sizes: consumed as MPFS_DDR_*_LENGTH defsyms only. Note DDR_Present is
# NOT here -- mpfs_config_checks.ads reads it, so it is tagged.
ddr_cached_kb
ddr_noncached_kb
ddr_wcb_kb
# Main stack size: consumed as the __stack_size defsym only.
main_stack_size
